Z||000001||cadaver||08-17-2001||12:08 AM||||I replaced mine at one time with a 5 1/4 inch woofer from a speaker shop. Then I replaced it with an 8 inch woofer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||08-17-2001||08:35 AM||||If you're just wanting to replace the original speaker with a new one of the same size, go to <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com." TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com.</A>   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||08-17-2001||08:40 AM||||I believe Rodney Dickman sells a good replacement speaker. I don't have the link right now but a quick search on his name and you'll find it. I don't know about the amp.<P>I saved a couple of bucks and repaired my speaker. I bought an inexpensive speaker of the same size from Walmart and carefully removed the foam ring. I trimmed off the excess paper and used rubber contact cement to glue it to the original speaker. That was about a year ago and it's still working great. Total repair cost... less than $10.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||85ZainoGT||08-17-2001||05:16 PM||||what are we talking about? there is a subwoofer that came with the car? where? if not, where can I fit a sub in my car??? lol||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieronv||08-17-2001||05:52 PM||||85ZainoGT:<BR> Us poor guys that own a pre 86 car don't have a subwoofer built in. I have seen a lot of places to put a sub in our cars (behind the seat if short, aus's center console, in the passenger well, in the front compartment) the best way to look at is what do you want for convience. I don't want to loose my spare and I'm tall so what I did was to put a bazooka tube in the passenger side. I find that it hits hard and I can still carry a passenger. Also I can remove it easily. I have pictures of this on this link.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009358.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009358.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000006||85ZainoGT||08-17-2001||07:24 PM||||wow, thats an awesome set up you got there, now I jus need the money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  do you know if there are boxes that can fit somewhere? for 12's or 10's?||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieronv||08-17-2001||09:05 PM||||I've seen people put 10's and 12's behind the seat but you have to move the seats really far forward also when I measured the cubic feet of the cabin the ideal size of subs are 8 inch, if you want a balanced sound from your stereo. Try to get a hold of a members car in the area that has a sub to hear what they have and adjust the size and placement of your sub. Also do a search for subs and stereo there is a lot of ideas out there.<P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
